  "note": "The one owner of how each floor is dressed. Godot reads it (FloorRecipes) and validates it at load. skinWeights: how often a district wears each skin on this floor (the same four skins godot/resources/default-skin-mix.json lists; a district draws one by weight, so a floor can wear one skin twice). light: torch is the colour every warm practical leans toward and by how much (it must stay a warm light), accent the colour every cold light and glow leans toward (it must stay a cold light), practicalDensity scales how readily a room gets its second pool, cold grate or hall torch (above 1 more lights, below 1 fewer); strength multiplies the energy of every torch, lantern and grate on the floor, and its square root their range (0.5 to 3); fullStrength, when set, replaces strength in Full quality only (0.5 to 5, since dark floors answer light less in Full quality; Retro never reads it; the lead's November 17 ruling: rooms that leave Opal's self-lit glass are lifted by light, never by paler stone). roomKinds: a multiplier on each room theme's weight in godot/resources/room-themes.json (hall is the plain room; 0 keeps a kind off this floor). roomShape: the floor's room-shape rule, recorded only until a later lane builds it. masonrySet names a look in godot/resources/masonry/masonry-sets.json (the floor's world-space masonry; null keeps the skins' own floors and walls; lane masonry-pilot built Floor 4's look, floor4-ashlar-flagstone, and it is switched off until big-flag layouts: the scanned stones read busier than the slabs at the game camera; the review switch STRANGEDEEP_MASONRY_PREVIEW shows it). roomFloorings (lane floor-textures, November 17; Adam: \"the textures should be considered per room identity\"): a room kind (hall, library, crypt, camp, armory, shrine, workshop) to the flooring and colourway its rooms wear, both named in godot/resources/masonry/masonry-sets.json floorings; a kind not named keeps the floor's own masonry or skin; STRANGEDEEP_ROOM_FLOORS=off is the rollback. edgeTreatment, overlaySet and heroSetPiece are empty slots that later lanes fill. naturalDressing: how readily each room gets each kind of natural dressing (lane rocks-flowers, November 17; RoomThemes.RocksFlowers.cs): rocks are loose stone fields, rubble the heaps at a wall's foot, roots the root masses breaking the floor at wall bases, flowers the unwilting flowers; each is the expected count in a room of about 40 squares (a bigger room more), flowers growing with each room's distance from the arrival so they lead on. 0 keeps a kind off the floor. Which variants each kind draws is godot/resources/room-themes.json, natural. A floor below the last recipe uses the last recipe.",
